{"id":"PPG_V2.80_beta1__compounds__set_face_ID_tags","collection":"PPG_V2.80_beta1","category":"compounds","source_path":"PPG_V2.80_beta1/compounds/set_face_ID_tags.json","root_names":["PPG::set_face_ID_tags"],"counts":{"nodes":18,"connections":43,"values":15,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Set the face tags base of the face ID. The resulting tags are numbers (the face ID) with an optional prefix.","documentation_search":"Set Faces ID Tags Set the face tags base of the face ID. The resulting tags are numbers (the face ID) with an optional prefix. Inputs Mesh The input geometry. Tag Expression A simple space separated list of face tag names to select faces of the input mesh for the cutting. You can use \\ in the names as a wildcard. Face Indices A list of numbers (uint) of faces to use for the cutting. Invert After adding the faces from tag expressions and indices together this will invert the selection to all other faces of the mesh. This flag is also helpful if there are not face tags in the object. Tag Prefix Postfix Tag Prefix Prefix for the new tag. Tag Postfix Postfix for the new tag. Store as Reference NOTE: A prefix is necessary to use this option. If this option in turned ON the points of the selected faces and their unique face tags are stored in the object for later use. The goal is to store information about the size and orientation of these faces for later use. The descendants of these faces can later access this information in the node \"PPG multi cut\". Tutorial","port_names":["face_indices","inherit_source_tag","invert","mesh","out_object","store_as_reference","tag_expression","tag_postfix","tag_prefix"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::build_array","Core::Logic::and","Core::Logic::if","Core::Logic::not","Core::Object::set_property","Core::String::build_string","Core::String::number_to_string","Core::String::string_empty","Core::String::string_join","PPG::get_face_indices","PPG::get_points_per_face","PPG::set_face_tag","Unknown","rename_with_inherit"],"dependencies_search":["PPG::get_face_indices","PPG::get_points_per_face","PPG::set_face_tag"],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"PPG::set_face_ID_tags","uri_imported":null,"is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/ENU/set_face_ID_tags.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Store face points and tags as reference info"}]},"documentation_file":"PPG_V2.80_beta1/docs/ENU/set_face_ID_tags.md","documentation":"# Set Faces ID Tags\nSet the face tags base of the face ID.<br>\nThe resulting tags are numbers (the face ID) with an optional prefix.\n\n## Inputs\n\n### Mesh\nThe input geometry.\n\n### Tag Expression\nA simple space separated list of face tag names to select faces of the input mesh for the cutting.<br>\nYou can use \\* in the names as a wildcard.\n\n### Face Indices\nA list of numbers (uint) of faces to use for the cutting.\n\n### Invert\nAfter adding the faces from tag expressions and indices together this will invert the selection to all other faces of the mesh.\nThis flag is also helpful if there are not face tags in the object.\n\n## Tag Prefix Postfix\n### Tag Prefix\nPrefix for the new tag.<br>\n\n### Tag Postfix\nPostfix for the new tag.<br>\n\n### Store as Reference\nNOTE: A prefix is necessary to use this option.<br>\nIf this option in turned ON the points of the selected faces and their unique face tags are stored in the object for later use.<br>\nThe goal is to store information about the size and orientation of these faces for later use. The descendants of these faces can later access this information in the node \"PPG_multi_cut\".\n\n## Tutorial\n\n<br><br>","ports":[{"name":"mesh","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"tag_expression","direction":"input","type":"string","default":"*"},{"name":"face_indices","direction":"input","type":null},{"name":"invert","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"false"},{"name":"inherit_source_tag","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"false"},{"name":"tag